Hi there, it's been a long time since my first ascension. Here's the
second.

I avoided some mistakes I made on first ascension, commited new ones...
I guess I'm an eternal learner!.

I don't take notes (first mistake!), so I don't remember much the early
game. Just on second level was a shop with some handy boots of speed (I
can't believe the rng gave such a gift without killing me); further
down there was a polymorph trap, the little dog had been killed long
ago (sigh! :_( ), I managed to get another pet and polymorph it using
the trap... a blue dragon, not bad at all... :-). As ever, used the
same lame thing to let the pet kill shopkeepers to get gold for
protection. I lost the pet on a level teleport trap, he was gone to
level 1, and when I found him he was no longer tame, even peaceful... i
let him survive in memory of the good times we spent toguether.

I got an early wand of wishing, so I got the mandatory (for me, of
course) silver dragon scale mail. Eventually got polymorphed (then I
hadn't the ring of polymorph control whitch I used almost the whole
game), turned into a silver dragon... by then I was a female (playing
with amulets of change), so I laid down some eggs, and there was my
lovely children. Only one survived, he's still some levels up medusa.

So I was having a lot of wishes, started wishing for some quest
artifacts... Just another mistake, good way to lose some wishes.

I had heard about some thing named pudding farming, so I tried what was
it about... It's just a lame trick, buy you know, I'M LAME!. So I got
some spellbooks... polymorph! :-). Had to kill (or make kill, don't
remember) the priest of molloch in the valley of the dead for his robe,
had also a helm of brilliance. Had my amulet of life saving, gaunltets
of dexterity.. ready to go!.... but wait! before that I managed to make
two mistakes again (I'm a king at this!)
-If I put a bag of holding into another bag of holding will the weight
decrea... BANG!
-Agh! a purple worm!! I'll throw him some +5 blessed rustproof orcish
daggers... wait a minute, i can polymorph him into a friendlier
creature... oh, my! the daggers turned into clubs, maces...

I was using a small shield, some armor is always wellcome, but then I
saw it was wiser to use two weapons: a silver saber and frost brand.

So that was my life: farming on level 4, and going down to gehenom to
dig the walls of the mazes, just to make the rodney run cleaner. I
managed to get killed twice:
-On the valley of the dead: I ate a dragon/giant corpse (don't remember
well) and just after a titanothere... (WHAT A STUPID WAY TO LOSE AN
AMULET OF LIFE SAVING!)
-Second time: I thought that magical protection from a robe and
reflection from the armor was enough for finger of death... a titan
politely explained me that it was not.

So my last 2 wishes were for an amulet of life saving (the spellbook of
polymorph was faint, and faint...) and for that cloak of magic
protection every orc should have. Prepared some daggers, some food,
tamed some purple worms and went for rodney.

That *@#!!! killed all 3 worms without letting me delight with the
sound of a BUUUUURRRRP!, I zapped him with one of the two only wands of
death I had (had some more, but were on the bag I blew up). Went to the
vibrating square, charmed some dragons, got the amulet, killed rodney
some times...

the food and the daggers were in my pudding farm, so there I let all
what was useful, picked all wands of digging I could carry, the 5
scrolls of gold detection I had, a helm of opposite alignment, some
holy water.
Once in the planes zapped some forgotten spell to get confused (Someone
tell me why this is a bad idea, It has always worked for me) and
reached the final stage. As always, the first altar was not my god's...
considered turning into a neutral, but Kos had been quite kind with
me...
As ever, went to the second altar... it wasn't my god's, It was
lawful... me lawful??? NEVER!. So as always seem to happen to me,
headed to the last one. I managed to lose most daggers, I threw them to
the riders and didn't mind to pick'em up. It actually doesn't matter
when you're about to become a demi-god.

sacrificed the amulet, and that was all. Here's the log.

